IO-21: reject a time pattern with the wrong number of factors

handle_patterns() appended whatever factors a [PATTERNS] entry held and
nothing compared the count with the 12, 7, 24 or 24 factors a MONTHLY, DAILY,
HOURLY or WEEKEND pattern needs; a missing factor acted as 1.0. Check every
pattern's count in resolve_cross_references(), next to the check of the
pattern names, and report error 237, as the 5.3.0 patch does.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-21_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/ErrorCodes.cpp b/src/engine/core/ErrorCodes.cpp
index 41a0f4b..51ae73f 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/ErrorCodes.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/ErrorCodes.cpp
@@ -125,6 +125,7 @@ static const std::unordered_map<int, const char*>& error_table() {
         {231, "Transect %s has no depth."},
         {233, "invalid math expression."},
         {235, "invalid infiltration parameters."},
+        {237, "wrong number of factors for Time Pattern %s."},
 
         // File I/O
         {301, "files share same names."},
diff --git a/src/engine/core/ErrorCodes.hpp b/src/engine/core/ErrorCodes.hpp
index 58441c6..cfac09e 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/ErrorCodes.hpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/ErrorCodes.hpp
@@ -133,6 +133,7 @@ enum ErrorCode : int {
     ERR_TRANSECT_NO_DEPTH       = 231,  ///< Transect %s has no depth
     ERR_MATH_EXPR               = 233,  ///< invalid math expression
     ERR_INFILTRATION            = 235,  ///< invalid infiltration parameters
+    ERR_PATTERN_FACTORS         = 237,  ///< wrong number of factors for Time Pattern %s
 
     // --- File I/O (301–363) ---
     ERR_FILE_NAME               = 301,  ///< files share same names
diff --git a/src/engine/input/PostParseResolver.cpp b/src/engine/input/PostParseResolver.cpp
index 807f527..f47860f 100644
--- a/src/engine/input/PostParseResolver.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/input/PostParseResolver.cpp
@@ -2376,6 +2376,17 @@ void resolve_cross_references(SimulationContext& ctx) {
             check(ctx.dwf_inflows.pat3[ui]);
             check(ctx.dwf_inflows.pat4[ui]);
         }
+
+        // IO-21: a pattern needs exactly 12 MONTHLY, 7 DAILY or 24 HOURLY /
+        // WEEKEND factors; a missing one would silently act as 1.0.
+        for (int k = 0; k < ctx.patterns.count(); ++k) {
+            const auto uk = static_cast<std::size_t>(k);
+            const int type = ctx.patterns.types[uk];
+            const std::size_t need = (type == 0) ? 12 : (type == 1) ? 7 : 24;
+            if (type >= 0 && ctx.patterns.factors[uk].size() != need)
+                ctx.errors.push_back(format_error(openswmm::ERR_PATTERN_FACTORS,
+                                                  ctx.patterns.names[uk]));
+        }
     }
 
     // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
